Item 06 is done and marked `[x]`; items 07 and 08 remain, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE`. Nothing committed, nothing written to `solutions/`.

**What iteration 6 had left.** A complete module, tests and a tables run, but the run was never read. Its classifier tables were invalid: every model scored 1.000 because the study's own label columns had been swept into the "structure" feature set by an every-numeric-column selector. The tree split on `y` and the EBM ranked `y` and `gap` as its top two terms.

**What I did.**
- Fixed the leak in `learning/bound_gap.py`: feature sets are built from the feature-group names, and `feature_sets` now refuses any set holding a label or an upper bound. Added a size-free feature set, a treewidth-ceiling table with two theorem checks, and per-instance simplicial counts and randomised treewidth upper bounds for the ten drawn instances.
- Tests: 12 in `tests/test_bound_gap.py` (three new). Full suite 753 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed, 79 s.
- Re-ran the study (122 s), wrote `reports/ml_nature.md` §6, the PROGRESS entry, and marked the item.

**Findings.**
- Gap ≥ 2 never occurs below 20 customers. Structure beats density-and-size in every row under the file ∪ class grouping, so the kill criterion is not met. The margin is in average precision (EBM 0.35 → 0.77; within fixed-size cells 0.54 → 0.81), not AUC, because a gap of two is first of all a large-and-sparse phenomenon. The lower bounds add nothing to the classifier.
- At fixed size the gap instances are sparser with more dispersed degrees, and the observed-over-expected graph density sits at chance. Nothing about the graph is anomalous given the matrix; it is the sparsity itself.
- The mechanism is structural. Three of the four components of the bound are treewidth lower bounds, and on 131 of the 338 gap ≥ 2 instances pathwidth provably exceeds treewidth, so they could not be tight under any budget. Only the expansion bound ever exceeds the treewidth ceiling.
- The ten smallest (all 20×10, all re-certified) are trees of cliques with branching: ten small product-cliques glued at a few hub customers with a fringe of single-product customers. Warwick 871 is the clean case, with treewidth exactly 3 and pathwidth 5.

**Next** is item 07; an earlier iteration left `learning/distil.py` committed, so it should be read before rebuilding. A note for later studies is in PROGRESS.md: any study that adds a label column must build its feature sets from the group names, not from the every-numeric-column selectors.

